/T (Joe E.)
/Contents (Lithium abundances, \(as measured in metal-poor stars in the Milky Way's stellar halo\), show no relation to the passage of time. More technically, Li/H ratios did not conformally increase with Fe/H ratios, instead levelling off in a so-called 'spite plateau'. This means that while iron is continually produced with Galactic/stellar nucleosynthesis, lithium seems to be overwhelmingly primordial.)
/CreationDate (D:20250221121744-08'00')
/M (D:20250221121744-08'00')
